config OSAL
	bool
	default y
	select EVENTS
	select DYNAMIC_THREAD
	select DYNAMIC_THREAD_ALLOC
	select THREAD_STACK_INFO
	select THREAD_NAME
	help
	  Hard Kconfig requirements of the Zephyr OSAL backend
	  (components/osal/src/zephyr/osal.c). These are not
	  application-specific tunables: osal.c will not compile or behave
	  correctly on Zephyr without them, so the module selects them
	  unconditionally instead of relying on every consumer to copy them
	  into its own prj.conf.

	  CONFIG_LOG is deliberately not selected here: osal_log.c degrades
	  gracefully to no-ops without it, so whether to enable logging is
	  left as an application choice.

	  CONFIG_HEAP_MEM_POOL_SIZE and CONFIG_MAIN_STACK_SIZE are also not
	  set here: how much heap/stack OSAL needs depends on how many
	  threads/mailboxes/etc. the application creates through it, so
	  sizing them is an application integration decision, not a fixed
	  module requirement.
